  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Toushir's connected wholesale workspace",
    "overview": "The supplied Figma file `4IffhmSg2gHg82narIGfMF` remains the visual authority. This document records how that existing world is implemented in the wholesaler workspace and merchant/courier applications: original Toushir assets, DM Sans, white surfaces, mint selection, bright green actions and dense operational content. It extends that world; it does not establish a replacement identity. Preserve the proportions of the original mark and navigation assets, and the identity of sourced product packaging.\n\nThe atmosphere is quiet and practical. Headings orient the user, tonal panels group work, and restrained status colours make current state visible. A commercial action has an explicit label and outcome. Unknown prices remain unconfirmed, demo content stays labelled, and illustrations never masquerade as observations. The source evidence is `apps/web/src/style.css`, `apps/web/src/main.tsx`, `apps/mobile/src/theme.ts`, `apps/mobile/src/components.tsx`, `apps/mobile/src/Merchant.tsx`, `apps/mobile/src/Driver.tsx` and the DM Sans font registration in `apps/mobile/App.tsx`.\n\nThis is a source-grounded system record. Exact acceptance of all 265 Figma states, native runtime acceptance and domain/security acceptance have separate evidence; they are not certified by this document.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Original Figma identity and assets across three operational workspaces.",
      "White and soft neutral surfaces with mint selection and green actions.",
      "Compact DM Sans hierarchy with tabular financial data on the web.",
      "Flat content, gently curved containers and transient overlays.",
      "Explicit commercial states, demo labels and observed-data boundaries."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The State Has a Label Rule",
        "body": "Colour supports a named state; it never supplies the only explanation of a commercial outcome.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Category Meaning Rule",
        "body": "Keep beverage mint and fresh/milk aqua in the merchant rail; extend other categories from the existing neutral treatment rather than inventing a rainbow.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Family Rule",
        "body": "Extend the DM Sans hierarchy and the confirmed Figma text styles before introducing another typeface.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Contained Overflow Rule",
        "body": "Preserve readable operational data and contain horizontal table scrolling within its panel.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Observed Position Rule",
        "body": "Keep illustrative depot geometry distinct from authorized GPS; never turn an animation, missing signal or stale observation into a live-location claim.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** extend the supplied Figma world and preserve the original Toushir assets and sourced packaging identity.",
      "**Do** use green actions, mint selection and labelled semantic statuses on quiet neutral surfaces.",
      "**Do** retain beverage mint, fresh/milk aqua and neutral unselected categories in the merchant rail.",
      "**Do** preserve keyboard focus, native touch targets, safe areas and contained table scrolling.",
      "**Do** label demo content, unknown commercial values, stale GPS and illustrative depot geometry explicitly.",
      "**Do** keep preparation, custody, receipt, payment and reconciliation visibly distinct."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** replace unknown prices with zero or present catalogue provenance as an approved commercial offer.",
      "**Don't** imply that illustrative 3D or a missing/stale GPS signal is a live observed position.",
      "**Don't** spread overlay shadows across flat operational panels or replace original icons with decorative text glyphs.",
      "**Don't** infer exact Figma-screen acceptance, native execution or domain/security acceptance from this design record."
    ]
  }
}
